File Index

/EnginePage.tsx
Purpose: Engine tab (Phase 15) — global infra action (own state/polling, no useAreaWorkbench dependency, same category as AccessPage), a THIRD action beyond Hot Reload/Copyover (those apply content changes; this applies code changes). Polls GET /api/rebuild/status every 3s; capabilities().rebuildEnabled gates whether the page shows anything beyond "not enabled," rebuildStatus().canTrigger gates whether the trigger button renders at all (hidden entirely for a non-eligible caller rather than shown and left to 403). A failed poll (the container being recreated mid-rebuild is expected, not an error) shows a "Reconnecting…" banner and KEEPS the last known status on screen — never treated as "the rebuild failed"; only a successfully-read status.phase === 'failed' means that. The trigger button is behind a window.confirm whose copy explicitly warns the builder tool itself will disconnect and reconnect partway through (not copyover's "brief pause" framing) since this action recreates mud-builder-server itself, unlike copyover. 2026-07-26 (UX polish pass): the dismissible toast (line ~105) now renders via the shared features/shared/Toast.js component — also fixed it becoming click-to-dismiss, which it wasn't before (the hand-rolled `<p>` had no onClick). The two OTHER `mb-toast mb-toast--err`-styled blocks (the "Reconnecting…" banner and a persistent status.error line) are intentionally NOT on the shared component — they're condition-driven persistent banners, not one-shot dismissible toasts, and dismissing them by click would be wrong (they should stay as long as the condition holds). Step 6 (error-message audit): both catch blocks (initial capabilities load, trigger's own catch) previously surfaced the raw exception message with no context at all — now prefixed "server unreachable: "/"rebuild trigger failed: " respectively, matching the "X failed: <message>" convention already used everywhere else in the app.

/EnginePage.test.tsx
Purpose: Engine tab tests: "feature not enabled" message with no button, "no permission" message when canTrigger is false, trigger→confirm→POST→status update happy path, confirm-declined never calls the API, and the key regression guard — a failed poll (mocked fetch rejection) shows the reconnecting banner while KEEPING the last known in-progress status on screen, never flipping to a "failed" state (uses jest.useFakeTimers + advanceTimersByTime to trigger the second poll deterministically).
